### Kubernetes Platform

K3s

### Kyverno Rule Type

Mutate

### Description

The logs indicate evaluation errors for resource kind that the policy should not even act on.

### Steps to reproduce

Create policy:
```yaml
apiVersion: policies.kyverno.io/v1
kind: NamespacedMutatingPolicy
metadata:
  name: longhorn-add-nixos-path
  namespace: longhorn-system
  annotations:
    policies.kyverno.io/title: Add Environment Variables from ConfigMap
    policies.kyverno.io/subject: Pod
    policies.kyverno.io/category: Other
    policies.kyverno.io/description: |
      Longhorn invokes executables on the host system, and needs to be aware of the host systems PATH.
      This modifies all deployments such that the PATH is explicitly set to support NixOS based systems.
      Original source: https://github.com/longhorn/longhorn/issues/2166#issuecomment-1293268590 Changed from legacy Policy to NamespacedMutatingPolicy.
spec:
  failurePolicy: Fail
  matchConstraints:
    resourceRules:
      - apiGroups: ['']
        apiVersions: ['v1']
        operations: ['CREATE']
        resources: ['pods']
  mutations:
    - patchType: JSONPatch
      jsonPatch:
        expression: |
          (has(object.spec.initContainers) ?
            object.spec.initContainers.map(c,
              !has(c.envFrom) ?
                JSONPatch{
                  op: "add",
                  path: "/spec/initContainers/" + string(object.spec.initContainers.indexOf(c)) + "/envFrom",
                  value: []
              } : null
            ).filter(p, p != null) : []
          ) +
          (has(object.spec.initContainers) ?
            object.spec.initContainers.map(c,
              object.spec.initContainers.indexOf(c)
            ).map(idx,
              JSONPatch{
                op: "add",
                path: "/spec/initContainers/" + string(idx) + "/envFrom/-",
                value: {"configMapRef": {"name": "longhorn-nixos-path"}}
              }
            ) : []
          ) +
          (has(object.spec.containers) ?
            object.spec.containers.map(c,
              !has(c.envFrom) ?
                JSONPatch{
                  op: "add",
                  path: "/spec/containers/" + string(object.spec.containers.indexOf(c)) + "/envFrom",
                  value: []
              } : null
            ).filter(p, p != null) : []
          ) +
          object.spec.containers.map(c,
            object.spec.containers.indexOf(c)
          ).map(idx,
            JSONPatch{
              op: "add",
              path: "/spec/containers/" + string(idx) + "/envFrom/-",
              value: {"configMapRef": {"name": "longhorn-nixos-path"}}
            }
          )
```

2. Create a deployment in the namespace of the `NamespacedMutatingPolicy`: `kubectl create deployment test --image nginx`
3. Observe logs about failed evaluation for kind deployment

### Expected behavior

Policy is only applied to pods.

