### Description

this line is unreachable - https://github.com/kyverno/kyverno/blob/0fe91382401630df2c26c5525dd9eb9c0df1b0ef/pkg/utils/kube/secret.go#L60
This code might be unreachable:
```
		if err != nil {
			return *resource, fmt.Errorf("unable to convert object from secret: %w", err)
		}
```
because after cheking the of value `err`  in this line:
```
		if err != nil {
			return *resource, fmt.Errorf("unable to convert metadata to map: %w", err)
		}
```
the value of `err` doesn't chaghe after first condition.

I discribe this fragment of code
```
		metadata, err := datautils.ToMap(resource.Object["metadata"])
		if err != nil {
			return *resource, fmt.Errorf("unable to convert metadata to map: %w", err)
		}
		updatedMeta := updateSecret["metadata"].(map[string]interface{})
		if err != nil {
			return *resource, fmt.Errorf("unable to convert object from secret: %w", err)
		}
```
This is not critical mistake, but it is unnecessary code and it can make harder the process of analyzing error message

